{"thought":"The existing tests in `tests/test_nativetypes.py` cover various aspects of the `NativeEnvironment` and its rendering capabilities. I will add a new test specifically for the bug described in issue #1701, which involves rendering a template that causes a `TypeError` due to an integer being used where a string is expected.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
from jinja2.nativetypes import NativeEnvironment

@pytest.fixture
def env():
    return NativeEnvironment()

def test_type_error_sequence_item(env):
    template = '{% block test %}{% for i in range(1) %}{{ loop.index }}{% endfor %}{% endblock %}{{ self.test() }}'
    with pytest.raises(TypeError, match='sequence item 0: expected str instance, int found'):
        env.from_string(template).render()"}}
